ype {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315204} {:answer/id #uuid "1786b331-60b2-5af9-afb3-9241c93e2af3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315252} {:answer/id #uuid "31852bd8-44e7-5955-8bea-f07a0732c4ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315403} {:answer/id #uuid "61e9e7e7-2c5a-53ab-a2a9-9bde7e323240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315667} {:answer/id #uuid "b29f537c-407a-5fdf-b8fa-73b1321dd3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b29f537c-407a-5fdf-b8fa-73b1321dd3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316129} :answer-field/id #uuid "610123c1-85f6-5d37-a07c-e1988e3bea4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316776} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f6dbc93-1b83-5d25-acd9-9c2c8535de5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315481} {:answer/id #uuid "92e83496-3189-5e03-8cde-441b6833ff0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "periodic" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315939} {:answer/id #uuid "dc308651-5eb0-524d-b97d-db4942257375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316343} {:answer/id #uuid "e52ac4aa-e503-5d1f-b967-da2347d2b2d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f6dbc93-1b83-5d25-acd9-9c2c8535de5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315481} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f03cf21-0038-533a-aab9-c6147ed7f920" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "637c8c06-b50d-580c-8555-a7f2b7fa591e" :question/math-academy-id "q-342023" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=8x$ defined on $[-2,2).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $4$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=4{x}^{2}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n8x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an odd function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and we are already given the coefficients ${b}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-2,2).$ \nTherefore, the $4$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}8t\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ [4{t}^{2}]_{0}^{x} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\cdot [-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{2})]_{0}^{x} \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dc4a3af-4483-521b-bb70-d53ecf298569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550553} {:answer/id #uuid "6dac34b7-0afe-57b3-92dd-0f1fe22e6081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dc4a3af-4483-521b-bb70-d53ecf298569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550553} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c63119-6c8c-562e-abc9-23fca39a632c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80ea76ea-89c9-5952-ae08-cee6ace28d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550695} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7734d0-53ef-5456-8980-faad9723c723" :answer/type {:db/