nswer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6acce05c-927e-54a3-ab7e-dea3332ed930" :question/math-academy-id "q-342257" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/64/64b557365c3642ae7a4206794080804bf2bbccb07230dfa46a4f415570f85329.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}-5x=-5(-2)=10\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}=\\frac{5}{2}(2)^{2}=10.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{true}$ since statements I, II, and III are all true.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/cd/cd37979eada411b68755dfa85ec3b1e22585df2bff5c4bdd4b27cf06463706d6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce3ead7-0b83-5eab-9199-842cc025d4a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315380} {:answer/id #uuid "3aca0239-27a6-5c5c-96b6-cc49183e0e6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3aca0239-27a6-5c5c-96b6-cc49183e0e6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315456} :answer-field/id #uuid "23e8c250-6052-5c7e-8aa2-842606a473e0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316630} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9b64430-e1a7-5018-92b8-5a440a98a30f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316254} {:answer/id #uuid "e273b80a-755a-5202-a33c-bd0bc03650fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9b64430-e1a7-5018-92b8-5a440a98a30f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316254} :answer-field/id #uuid "77492101-d1f7-5814-a922-e3f5920b6f11" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a302410-85bc-585f-8c2d-33efa2dd93cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315169} {:answer/id #uuid "54e399fb-cac3-5ef5-8d8c-7f48f901bbcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54e399fb-cac3-5ef5-8d8c-7f48f901bbcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315605} :answer-field/id #uuid "90e114c9-5c98-54b3-9ea6-3e2d144fa479" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316880} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99fd6e29-10e2-567b-83cb-3f7adddc1fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315979} {:answer/id #uuid "e7e38600-19e2-5b19-ab04-bf50f924692c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99fd6e29-10e2-567b-83cb-3f7adddc1fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315979} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfd358e2-ceac-5b84-a7b4-d64ad89516db" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3280171-70dd-50e2-8570-67e489365512" :question/math-academy-id "q-342406" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+1, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ -2, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/7c/7cfd6da222fb36d06be1153ac0e398e567f8b9fb8cd1cd9e21f1bb35ed131f8d.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}(x+1)=-2+1=-1\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}(-2)=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statements I and III are false.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/a5/a59fad69c9790a2b899c21fd730f779c28bc9b70f44a67851ad5ca92bff21951.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cf9be56-efa9-5355-8976-ae2a23fa9c57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425552} {:answer/id #uuid "518e2251-cc5d-5108-bce8-18685a7d6e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cf9be56-efa9-5355-8976-ae2a23fa9c57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425552} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f816e4e-cb4e-5a7e-a240-55ae